# Line endings for the generated artifacts that are compared byte for byte.
#
# sprites/catalog.json is written by scripts/art_library.js (saveCatalog),
# scripts/index_art_words.js and scripts/apply_topik_art.js, all of which emit
# `JSON.stringify(pack, null, 2) + '\n'` — LF, on every platform. Two suites then
# assert that the file on disk is exactly those bytes:
#
#   tests/test_art_library.js   catalogued headwords are current
#   tests/test_topik_art.js     TOPIK art is out of sync
#
# Without this line a Windows checkout under core.autocrlf=true materialises the
# file with CRLF, so both suites fail on a clean tree with a message that blames
# the content — which is identical. Running the generator they recommend rewrites
# the file as LF and the tests pass, until the next checkout restores CRLF and
# they fail again. CI never sees it: ubuntu-latest checks out LF either way.
#
# js/vocabArtMore.js and js/systems/economy.js are written by the same script and
# are deliberately absent here: apply_topik_art.js sniffs their existing newline
# and preserves it, so they match whatever the checkout produced.
#
# A new generated file that gets byte-compared belongs on this list.
sprites/catalog.json text eol=lf
